{{Quote|I&hellip;I killed them. I killed them all. They're dead, every single one of them. And not just the men, but the women and the children too. They're like animals, and I slaughtered them like animals.|Anakin Skywalker, on his slaughter of the Tusken Raiders|<ref name="Episode II" />}}
A '''Tusken Raider village''' was located in the [[desert]]s of the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] [[Tatooine]] prior to the [[Clone Wars]]. It was [[Mission to rescue Shmi Skywalker Lars|destroyed]] by [[Anakin Skywalker]] out of revenge for the [[death]] of his [[Parent|mother]], [[Shmi Skywalker Lars]].

==Description==
This camp was the home of a group of [[Tusken Raider]]s on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] [[Tatooine]]. The camp was located in the [[desert]] and was situated between a number of [[mountain]]s. It contained over two dozen huts that served as the dwellings of the Tusken group. The camp was lit by [[fire]]s outside a number of the huts.<ref name="Episode II" />

==History==
In [[22 BBY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> the Tusken Raiders who lived in this camp kidnapped [[Shmi Skywalker Lars]] from her [[Lars homestead|home]]. They took her to their camp, where she was brutally beaten and kept as a [[prisoner]] for one [[Standard month|month]]. Her son, [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Anakin Skywalker]], [[Mission to rescue Shmi Skywalker Lars|came]] to Tatooine to look for her. She [[Death|died]] in his arms and, having lost control of his emotions, Skywalker used [[Anakin Skywalker's first lightsaber|his]] [[lightsaber]] to kill every Tusken Raider in the camp.<ref name="Episode II" />

